course: dictionary
lesson: 9466
title: Startle and startled
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To startle someone is to surprise them suddenly, so that they jump or move quickly. Think of a loud bang that makes you leap out of your seat. Startle is a verb, so it changes form: startle, startles, startled, startling.
explain: Read this context: «A boy in Texas woke his hamster in the daytime by poking it; the startled hamster bit his finger hard.» The hamster was poked while it slept, so startled must mean it got a sudden fright. The clues around the word tell you its meaning.
explain: A startled look is a face that shows a sudden surprise, with eyes wide for a moment. Animals are often startled by sudden noise. «Horses startle at sudden noise», so in the countryside stay calm and quiet near animals, and do not startle dogs, horses or babies.
fact: Startle means to surprise or frighten someone suddenly.
fact: «Startled» means got a sudden small fright.
fact: «Startling» describes something that gives a sudden fright, like a startling noise.
fact: A startled animal may bite or kick, so move slowly and speak softly near animals.
fact: Useful phrases: «startled by» something, as in «startled by a sudden noise».
exercise: «The startled hamster bit his finger hard.» Why did the hamster bite? | It wanted to sleep all day | *It was poked awake suddenly and got a fright | It was very hungry for a snack | It was playing a game with the boy
exercise: Which word means to surprise someone suddenly so that they jump? | soothe | *startle | yawn | wander
exercise: «Horses startle at sudden noise.» What should you do near horses? | Throw stones to see them move | Run up to them quickly | Shout and wave your arms | *Keep calm and quiet so you do not startle them
test: «a startled look» means what? | *A sudden, surprised look | A calm, sleepy look | A cross, angry look | A happy, smiling look
test: In a story, a loud noise startles a deer. What happens next? | It stays still and waits for the noise to come back | It sings a song | *It jumps and runs off | It falls asleep in the grass
exam: Why must you not startle a dog? | *A startled animal may bite or kick | Dogs like being woken with a shout | Dogs cannot hear sudden noises | It makes dogs sleepy and slow
